@startuml Sequence_TwoPhase_Booking_Complete

title Sequence Diagram - Two-Phase Booking System with Payment\n(Request -> Confirm -> Payment -> Webhook)

actor User
participant "API Gateway" as API
participant "AuthMiddleware" as Auth
participant "BookingController" as Controller
participant "BookingService" as Service
participant "BookingRequest\nModel" as RequestModel
participant "Booking\nModel" as BookingModel
participant "PaymentService" as PayService
participant "StripePaymentStrategy" as StripeStrategy
participant "Stripe API" as Stripe
participant "Transaction\nModel" as TransModel
participant "WebhookService" as Webhook
participant "NotificationFactory" as NotifFactory
participant "Firebase" as FCM
database "MongoDB" as DB

== Phase 1: Request Booking (Create Temporary Lock) ==

User -> API: POST /api/v1/user/booking/request\n{vehicleId, startDate, endDate}
activate API

API -> Auth: Verify JWT Token
activate Auth
Auth --> API: userId extracted
deactivate Auth

API -> Controller: requestBooking(req, res)
activate Controller

Controller -> Service: requestBooking(userId, vehicleId, startDate, endDate)
activate Service

Service -> DB: Find User by userId
activate DB
DB --> Service: User found
deactivate DB

Service -> DB: Find Vehicle by vehicleId
activate DB
DB --> Service: Vehicle found
deactivate DB

Service -> DB: Check conflicts\n(Booking: status IN [pending, confirmed])
activate DB
DB --> Service: No conflicts
deactivate DB

Service -> DB: Check active BookingRequests\n(same vehicle, overlapping dates)
activate DB
DB --> Service: No active locks
deactivate DB

Service -> Service: Calculate days & priceQuote
note right
    days = (endDate - startDate) / 86400000
    priceQuote = days x pricePerDay
end note

Service -> Service: Generate requestToken
note right: crypto.randomBytes(32)

Service -> RequestModel: create(BookingRequest)
activate RequestModel
RequestModel -> DB: Save BookingRequest
activate DB
DB --> RequestModel: Saved
deactivate DB
RequestModel --> Service: bookingRequest
deactivate RequestModel

Service --> Controller: {requestToken, priceQuote, validUntil}
deactivate Service

Controller --> API: 200 OK\n{requestToken, priceQuote, days, validUntil}
deactivate Controller

API --> User: Quote Response
deactivate API

User -> User: Review Quote\n(has 15 minutes)

== Phase 2: Confirm Booking & Create Payment ==

User -> API: POST /api/v1/user/booking/confirm\n{requestToken}
activate API

API -> Auth: Verify JWT Token
activate Auth
Auth --> API: Authenticated
deactivate Auth

API -> Controller: confirmBookingWithPayment(req, res)
activate Controller

Controller -> Service: confirmBooking(requestToken)
activate Service

Service -> DB: Find BookingRequest\n(requestToken, status="active")
activate DB
DB --> Service: bookingRequest found
deactivate DB

Service -> Service: Check expiration\n(now < expiresAt?)
note right: Verify within 15-min window

Service -> DB: Re-check conflicts\n(double-check safety)
activate DB
DB --> Service: Still available
deactivate DB

Service -> BookingModel: create(Booking)
activate BookingModel
BookingModel -> DB: Save Booking\n(status: "pending")
activate DB
DB --> BookingModel: Saved
deactivate DB
BookingModel --> Service: booking
deactivate BookingModel

Service -> RequestModel: Update status = "confirmed"
activate RequestModel
RequestModel -> DB: Update
activate DB
DB --> RequestModel: Updated
deactivate DB
deactivate RequestModel

Service --> Controller: {booking, priceQuote}
deactivate Service

Controller -> PayService: createPaymentIntent(priceQuote, "usd", userId, bookingId)
activate PayService

PayService -> StripeStrategy: processPayment(amount, currency, {userId, bookingId})
activate StripeStrategy

StripeStrategy -> StripeStrategy: Convert metadata to strings
note right
    Stripe requires string values
    Convert ObjectIds to strings
end note

StripeStrategy -> Stripe: paymentIntents.create({amount, currency, metadata})
activate Stripe
Stripe --> StripeStrategy: paymentIntent\n{id, client_secret, status}
deactivate Stripe

StripeStrategy --> PayService: {id, clientSecret, status, provider}
deactivate StripeStrategy

PayService -> TransModel: create(Transaction)
activate TransModel
TransModel -> DB: Save Transaction\n(status: "Pending")
activate DB
DB --> TransModel: Saved
deactivate DB
TransModel --> PayService: transaction
deactivate TransModel

PayService --> Controller: {paymentIntent, transaction}
deactivate PayService

Controller --> API: 201 Created\n{booking, clientSecret, transactionId, amount}
deactivate Controller

API --> User: Confirm Response
deactivate API

== Payment Processing ==

User -> User: Enter Card Details\n(using Stripe.js)

User -> Stripe: Submit Payment\n(with clientSecret)
activate Stripe

Stripe -> Stripe: Process Card Payment

alt Payment Successful

    Stripe -> API: Webhook: payment_intent.succeeded
    activate API

    API -> Webhook: handleStripeWebhookEvent(event)
    activate Webhook

    Webhook -> DB: Find Transaction\n(providerPaymentId, status="Completed")
    activate DB
    DB --> Webhook: Not found (not duplicate)
    deactivate DB

    Webhook -> TransModel: Update status = "Completed"
    activate TransModel
    TransModel -> DB: Update
    activate DB
    DB --> TransModel: Updated
    deactivate DB
    deactivate TransModel

    Webhook -> BookingModel: Update status = "confirmed"
    activate BookingModel
    BookingModel -> DB: Update Booking
    activate DB
    DB --> BookingModel: Updated
    deactivate DB
    deactivate BookingModel

    Webhook --> API: Transaction updated
    deactivate Webhook

    API --> Stripe: 200 OK (webhook received)
    deactivate API

    Stripe --> User: Payment Success
    deactivate Stripe

    Webhook -> NotifFactory: createNotification("push")
    activate NotifFactory
    NotifFactory --> Webhook: PushNotification instance
    deactivate NotifFactory

    Webhook -> FCM: Send Push Notification
    activate FCM
    FCM --> User: "Booking Confirmed!"
    deactivate FCM

    User -> User: View Confirmed Booking

else Payment Failed

    Stripe -> API: Webhook: payment_intent.payment_failed
    activate API

    API -> Webhook: handleStripeWebhookEvent(event)
    activate Webhook

    Webhook -> TransModel: Update status = "Failed"
    activate TransModel
    TransModel -> DB: Update
    activate DB
    DB --> TransModel: Updated
    deactivate DB
    deactivate TransModel

    Webhook --> API: Transaction failed
    deactivate Webhook

    API --> Stripe: 200 OK
    deactivate API

    Stripe --> User: Payment Failed
    deactivate Stripe

    User -> User: Retry or Cancel

end

@enduml
